# `prompt-unmarked` for a function value in a widget function's result (ruling PT,
# soundness): `@Make` gives back a function that captures its argument `!told`, so a
# caller applying that function in the tick `!told` fires gets `!told`'s firing; its
# result is prompt in `!told`, and the type must say so.
# Expected text derived by hand; never run.
# Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*

@Make: fn !Nat -> @(fn !Nat -> @!Nat)
fn @Make !told:
    @ \|!ignored| @ !told
